tebelskis@msn.com (Joe Tebelskis) wrote in message news:<7340a1d5.0411171412.21db0f40@posting.google.com>...
> In a recent game I encountered and defeated my own ghost from an
> earlier game.  Is it considered unethical to refer to my notes from
> the end of that game to fully identify the items left at my own grave?

My vote is "not unethical," on the reasoning that it's not unethical
to use your actual *knowledge* of your ancestor's kit, and it's not
unethical to use notes within an individual game.  However, I would
probably throw away the notes anyway, because I think the game is more
fun without cross-lifetime bookkeeping.  I definitely wouldn't be
comfortable with taking notes for the sole purpose of id-ing stuff in
later bones files, it's too close to bones-scumming.

IMHO and VMMV of course.

